{#
  The one logout control, shared by every page that offers "Log out".

  Why a form and not a link:
    - Turbo 8 prefetches LINKS on hover; a GET to the logout path used to sign
      people out just by hovering. Forms are never prefetched.
    - A POST with a CSRF token stops other sites forcing a logout.
  LogoutRequestGuard is what enforces both; see that class for the full story.

  data-turbo="false": logout ends in a redirect to the identity provider (a
  different origin) for SSO users. Turbo submits forms with fetch(), which
  cannot follow that redirect, so this must be an ordinary full-page submit.
  It also means it works the same with JavaScript off.

  Variables (all optional):
    button_class  CSS classes for the button   (default: "button button--secondary")
    form_class    extra classes for the <form> (default: none)
    label         button text                  (default: "Log out")

  @see \Pixiekat\HMFPSearchToolBundle\EventListener\LogoutRequestGuard
#}
<form class="logout-form {{ form_class|default('') }}" method="post" action="{{ path('saml_logout') }}" data-turbo="false">
  <input type="hidden" name="_logout_token" value="{{ csrf_token('logout') }}">
  <button type="submit" class="{{ button_class|default('button button--secondary') }}">{{ label|default('Log out') }}</button>
</form>
